    },
    "message": "fix(analytics): capture cache tokens from message_delta; illustrate the Guide\n\nCached input never appeared for OpenRouter, and the reason was in my own\ncapture rather than the provider mapping.\n\nAnthropic-native upstreams report cache counters on message_start, so that is\nthe only place the capture looked. Everything translated from an OpenAI-shaped\nprovider learns them from the final usage chunk instead, which arrives on\nmessage_delta -- so the value was extracted correctly and then thrown away.\n\nProven against live OpenRouter: a repeated 4k-token prompt returns\nprompt_tokens 4011 with prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens 3968, the provider\nmaps that to cache_read_input_tokens 3968, and the request log now records\ntokens_in 4011 and cache_read_tokens 3968 -- a 98.9% hit rate that previously\nrecorded as nothing. Both event shapes are covered by tests.\n\nThe dashboard Guide was thin next to the README, mostly because it had no\nimages. Seven screenshots now ship inside the package and are served from a new\n/admin/img route that matches against the files actually bundled rather than\njoining a path, so a crafted name cannot escape the directory. A test asserts\nevery image the Guide references is bundled.\n\nThe Guide itself is rewritten to match the depth of the written guide:\nstep-by-step Claude Code and Claude Desktop tutorials with their screenshots,\nthe validation-failure table, model tier advice, web search including full page\ntext, how to read the cache columns, rotation, updating, and a security section\ncovering what binds where.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
